# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form — Web3Forms access key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where to get it:
#   1. Go to https://web3forms.com
#   2. Enter contact@jpmediagroups.com and submit
#   3. The key arrives at that address — paste it below
#
# The key is delivery-only: it names the inbox a submission is addressed to and
# nothing else. It cannot read past submissions, and Web3Forms refuses to send
# to any address other than the one the key was created for. It ends up in the
# browser bundle by design, exactly like a reCAPTCHA site key.
#
# `PUBLIC_` is required — Astro only exposes prefixed variables to client code.
#
# Also set this in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, for Production,
# Preview and Development. A variable that only exists locally means the live
# form reports "not configured yet" while it works fine on your machine.
#
# Leave it empty and the form refuses to send rather than pretending it did.
PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
